==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Drama Cats '''at level 10.

Evolves into '''Slapstick Cats''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
This duet forms a powerful, well-rounded frontline unit for your Cat army. A stronger but slower [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]], the Figure Skating Cats are best used in stacks to accumulate DPS quickly. They are very useful cats for almost any lineup, essentially the Super Rare equivalent of Paris Cat. However, in stages with lots of money, it's better to use Paris Cat since she can be stacked more, dealing more total damage. Later in the game, however, they will show their true value as they usually survive longer than Paris and provide more value for a single Figure Skating Cats compared to several Paris Cats, thanks to their better cost efficiency.

==='''True Form'''===
Slapstick Cats should be a first investment priority in [[Uncanny Legends]], for they are one of the best non-[[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber]] counters to [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relic]] enemies. Their usage stays the same, but their added abilities make them the go-to specialist for Relic enemies, not too differently than how [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]] and [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]] are used against their traits. Aside from this, their generalist midranger value is improved thanks to their improved stats.

==='''Talents'''===
The [[Weaken|weaken]] ability greatly improves Slapstick Cats' survivability against Relics, as well as that of the whole army when the effect triggers. Sadly, it's only a 20% chance at most, but it is still a great improvement, since they usually end up forming a stack, meaning that the ability is much more reliable than it first seems. The basic stat boosts are very good to have, but nothing special, while resistance to [[Slow|slow]] rarely makes a difference, as they are already fairly slow to begin with. [[Immune to Knockback|Knockback immunity]] is unlikely to be worth that much NP, if any at all; being immune to knockback would prevent certain enemies, notably [[M. Ost]], from pushing Slapstick Cats to safety whenever they get hit, doing more harm than good.

==='''Orb'''===
While Slapsticks would theoretically benefit from any Attack Up or Defense Up Orb, it is usually better to give them a Strong Up Orb vs Relic to maximize their speciality performance.

