==Trivia==
*The Slapstick Cats are based on manzai-style comedy duos, which consist of a silly man (forgetful and prone to misinterpretation) and a straight man (impatient and quick to correct errors). Their Japanese name, Nyandeyanen, is a portmanteau of ''nyan'' (Japanese onomatopoeia for the sound cats make) and ''nandeyanen'', a Kansai dialect phrase which can be translated as "What are you talking about" or "Are you kidding me," used in response to something the speaker finds absurd. This phrase (or a variation thereof) is frequently invoked by the "straight man" to berate the "silly man" and is often accentuated by a jab or smack to the head, sometimes with a paper fan prop.
**They may also be a reference to the comedy duo [[wikipedia:ja:宮川大助・花子|Daisuke and Hanako Miyakawa]], who have worn some very similar styles to Slapstick Cats [https://youtu.be/xl2ih0AqAQA when performing]. Unlike the Miyakawas, however, it is the male cat who wears glasses.

